# Where every game picture comes from

Publisher artwork, used to identify the game. Decision D116: this is the
publisher's copyright and trademark in a sold, unlicensed accessory, and the
owner accepted that risk. Delete this folder's `.png` files and every config
falls back to our own banner with nothing else changed.

Rules: official publisher-provided images only. The Steam store's own
capsules for the game's app id; for a game Steam does not sell, the
PlayStation Store's own art for the game's concept page (the publisher
uploads it, the same as a Steam capsule); or the publisher's press kit.
Never Wikipedia covers, fan sites, SteamGridDB or image search. A game with
no official source stays on our own banner and is listed under **Missing**.

These pictures live in the app only: the exe and the phone app carry this
folder, and nothing about a picture is ever sent to the Core (D120).

## One picture per shape the app draws (D121)

Every game has two pictures, because the app draws two shapes and a picture
cropped to the wrong shape loses its title (Black Ops II's banner, cropped
square, is the black middle of it).

| shape | the picture | where the app draws it |
|---|---|---|
| `wide` | Steam's header capsule, 460 x 215 (about 2.14:1), title included | the Overview banner, the Configs list, the new-config wizard's game list |
| `tall` | a 2:3 portrait cover, 600 x 900: Steam's library capsule, or the PlayStation Store's portrait banner | HOME's picture, and the small square in the More menu |

Every slot draws its picture WHOLE: contained over a blurred, darkened copy
of itself, so a picture whose shape is a little off (a 16:9 banner in a wide
slot, a 0.83:1 cover in a tall one) gets soft edges and never loses its
title. Nothing is stretched and nothing is cropped.

The size column is the size the PNG is saved at: the largest the app draws
that shape, capped by what the publisher offers, never scaled up. HOME's
picture is about 349 x 523 CSS pixels on a 393 x 852 phone; the biggest 2:3
cover Steam serves is 600 x 900, so that is the size. The wide picture is
drawn at most about 357 CSS pixels across (the Overview banner), and Steam's
460 x 215 header is kept as it was fetched; Steam's `header_2x.jpg`
(920 x 430) is the swap to make if the banner looks soft on a 3x phone.

